      {
        "id": 221498,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-08-17T14:33:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Voss coming out early is far better than Voss showing up right as you flip to phase 3. That is brutal, especially if you don’t have ways to lock the Oblivaeon deck down with either bird form reward, writhe, legacy, or Nightmist.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>My general strategy so far so far has been to just focus on scion control in phase 2 and have them all low enough that as soon as phase 3 hits (likely due to the countdown) that I can clear all scions instantly and not worry about anything but Oblivaeon. Not always possible depending on the devestation count, but certainly one that’s worked in some of my wins.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Speaking of devestation tokens, ever tried 3 rounds In a row of Hypersonic Assult in phase 2? I did. It was really good until the token pile lost us the game haha. I don’t recommend that strat. It’s one of the few ways to easily clean out Borr before he goes boom boom though.&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:54:11.599Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
